# Trivy vulnerabilities suppressions
# Add CVE IDs here to ignore them during container image scanning
#
# ── npm CLI bundled in the base image (tracked since 2026-09-28) ─────────────
# The runner stage only executes `server.js`; `npm`/`npx` are never invoked by
# the container, its HEALTHCHECK, or docker-compose. These findings resolve
# against npm 10.8.2's own dependency tree (pacote 18.0.6, tar 6.2.1,
# sigstore 2.3.1, glob 10.4.2, cross-spawn 7.0.3, brace-expansion 2.0.1,
# ip-address 9.0.5, minimatch 9.0.5) which ships inside the base image and is
# not part of the application's runtime dependency graph. The pinned Node line
# bundles npm and it cannot be patched below these versions without leaving
# that line, so they are tracked here rather than in the lockfile.
# (2026-10-01) The Dockerfile now uses node:24-slim; these IDs stay listed
# until a scan confirms the npm 11.x bundle no longer matches them.
#
# brace-expansion
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
# (2026-09-30) same npm-bundled brace-expansion 2.0.1 — DoS via crafted/nested
# brace patterns; only reachable through the npm CLI, which never runs.
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
